      'The first thing to know about this repository is that it changed identity. An IMPORTANT notice in the README states that the repo now hosts AutoRAG 2.0, a complete reimagining as a personal librarian agent for office work, while the original Python RAG AutoML tool for finding an optimal RAG pipeline continues in maintenance mode through pip install AutoRAG with bug fixes, dependency updates and PyPI releases. Anyone arriving expecting a pipeline-tuning library needs to read that notice before choosing this project. What replaces it is a genuinely local-first product: Dazzi is the app version, and the README describes hybrid keyword plus meaning search with a reranker that finds files by what is inside them, where every answer links the passage it came from. Search spans local documents and cloud drives through their synced folders, plus Slack, KakaoTalk, Discord, Telegram, WhatsApp, signed-in inboxes, GitHub, Obsidian, GitHub Gists, coding-agent sessions and photos. Around that sits a real file manager: Space-bar Quick Look for Markdown, code, PDF, video, audio, Office and HWP/HWPX, with HWP pages drawn locally by rhwp so Hancom Office is not required; tabs and split panes that keep their own state; duplicate detection powered by dupey that collapses final, final-v3 and (1) copies into one row tagged Latest, Similar or Identical; folder-watch automations that triage or organize new files; scheduled re-indexing that runs even while the app is closed; and remote access paired with a 6-digit code or QR. Privacy choices are explicit rather than implied: embeddings run on the machine, keys live in the OS encrypted store, and a remote embedder is opt-in. The limits are practical ones. You must index the sources you care about, several messengers and mailboxes need sign-in, remote access needs a tunnel and pairing, and the 2.0 pivot means older AutoRAG material on the web may describe a different tool entirely.',
    description:
      'AutoRAG Agent is an Apache-2.0 personal librarian agent described as finding, reading and citing anything on your computer, with an MIT-style TypeScript repository whose topics include agentic RAG, document parsing, embeddings, hybrid search, local-first operation, MCP, memory and knowledge base. Dazzi is the desktop app version for Mac and Windows, distributed at dazziapp.com or buildable from the companion AutoRAG-app repository, and is described as a real file manager rather than a chat window. Its feature list includes fast hybrid keyword plus meaning search with a reranker where every answer links its source passage; searching messengers, mail, Slack, KakaoTalk, Discord, Telegram, WhatsApp, GitHub and Obsidian alongside files; pressing Space for Quick Look across Markdown, code, PDF, video, audio, Office and HWP/HWPX; file-based automations that watch a folder and triage or organize new files; duplicate detection that groups final, final-v3 and (1) copies under Latest, Similar or Identical; remote access from a phone or another computer over Wi-Fi or an internet tunnel paired with a 6-digit code or QR; and tabs, split panes, light and dark mode, and Korean, English, Japanese and Simplified Chinese interfaces. In the app you can ask as you would ask a teammate and the librarian writes back with every claim linked to its passage, drag files, folders or links into a question to narrow scope, and use an Ask entry in the Finder and Explorer right-click menu. Cloud drives such as Google Drive, iCloud Drive, OneDrive and Dropbox are searched through their synced folders, and data stays in each tool\'s own storage. The Private by design section states that semantic indexing runs on MinSync\'s local Qwen3-Embedding-0.6B engine with 1024 dimensions, that AutoRAG owns no embedding model, and that file contents are never sent to a remote embedder unless a remote minSync.embedder is explicitly configured. API keys and sign-in tokens live in the system\'s encrypted store rather than a config file, and users can bring their own provider key or use a hosted Dazzi Models plan. For agent builders, an autorag-lite-setup skill is documented as giving a coding agent model-free search over files, with manual installation and agent setup guides in docs/installation.md and docs/agent-setup.md.',
